From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Subject: [PATCH] iio: magnetometer: add MagnaChip MXM1120 Hall sensors

The pop-up front camera of the OnePlus 7 Pro and 7T Pro reports its
position through two MagnaChip MXM1120 Hall sensors on QUPv3 SE1
(0x0c upper, 0x0d lower), supplied by PM8150L L7 and L8. Check device
ID 0x9c, select 10-bit 80 Hz operation and expose polling raw reads
through IIO, plus an IIO channel provider (#io-channel-cells) for the
pop-up motor driver.

Source: hotdog-linux-bringup (https://github.com/Sr-0w/hotdog-linux-bringup,
commit 47087509c428), aports/device/testing/linux-oneplus-hotdog-mainline616/0103
with the binding as amended by 0104; device-tree hunks left out.

rc4 rebase on v7.0.0-sm8150-rc3: the Kconfig and Makefile hunks are moved
past the MMC5633 entry that 7.0 added. Driver content is unchanged.
Source-only: not compiled in this patch. Keep the DT nodes gated until
the Hall readings are measured (docs/motor-procedure.md).

Nura-Category: upstream-feature
Nura-Origin: hotdog-linux-bringup 0103/0104 (Robin Snyders)
Upstream-Status: not in mainline v7.2 (driver and binding absent)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/magnetometer/magnachip,mxm1120.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/magnetometer/magnachip,mxm1120.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e2962ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/magnetometer/magnachip,mxm1120.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/iio/magnetometer/magnachip,mxm1120.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: MagnaChip MXM1120 Hall effect magnetic position sensor
+
+maintainers:
+  - Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: magnachip,mxm1120
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  label:
+    description: Human-readable sensor position
+
+  "#io-channel-cells":
+    const: 0
+
+  vdd-supply:
+    description: Analog sensor supply
+
+  vio-supply:
+    description: I/O supply
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - vdd-supply
+  - vio-supply
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    i2c {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
+
+        magnetometer@c {
+            compatible = "magnachip,mxm1120";
+            reg = <0x0c>;
+            #io-channel-cells = <0>;
+            label = "camera-popup-up";
+            vdd-supply = <&vreg_hall_3p0>;
+            vio-supply = <&vreg_hall_1p8>;
+        };
+    };
